From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prarit Bhargava <prarit@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip Socket#connect timeout test in isolated environments.

The Socket#connect timeout test expects IO::TimeoutError when connecting
to 192.0.2.1:1 (TEST-NET-1), but in isolated CI environments without
network routing, it fails immediately with Errno::ENETUNREACH instead
of timing out.

Skip this test as it is environment-dependent.
---
 spec/ruby/library/socket/socket/connect_spec.rb | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/spec/ruby/library/socket/socket/connect_spec.rb b/spec/ruby/library/socket/socket/connect_spec.rb
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/spec/ruby/library/socket/socket/connect_spec.rb
+++ b/spec/ruby/library/socket/socket/connect_spec.rb
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ describe 'Socket#connect' do
 
     it "fails with timeout" do
+      skip "unreliable in isolated network environments"
       remote_addr = Socket.sockaddr_in(1, "192.0.2.1") # TEST-NET-1
 
       -> {
